## Tone Guidelines - CRITICAL: STRICT ADHERENCE REQUIRED

**YOU MUST STRICTLY FOLLOW THE TONE SPECIFIED BELOW. THE USER MUST CLEARLY FEEL THE DIFFERENCE BETWEEN TONES.**

{% if tone == "professional" %}
**PROFESSIONAL TONE - STRICT REQUIREMENTS:**

MANDATORY CHARACTERISTICS:
- Use formal, executive-level language throughout - NO casual expressions
- Focus exclusively on measurable results, strategic impact, and organizational value
- Use third-person perspective when describing employee ("John demonstrated," "his strategic approach")
- Maintain objective, data-driven language - NO emotional expressions
- Structure sentences formally with complex, sophisticated syntax
- Use business terminology: "strategic initiatives," "organizational objectives," "performance metrics," "stakeholder engagement"

REQUIRED PHRASES (must use at least 3-4):
- "demonstrated exceptional performance"
- "delivered outstanding results"
- "exceeded organizational objectives"
- "contributed significantly to"
- "strategic initiative"
- "organizational objectives"
- "performance metrics"
- "professional excellence"
- "leadership capabilities"
- "results-oriented approach"

FORBIDDEN PHRASES (DO NOT USE):
- "I am proud of" / "I'm proud of"
- "I am impressed" / "I'm impressed"
- "I am excited" / "I'm excited"
- "looking forward to"
- "truly impressive"
- "remarkable achievement"
- "fantastic"
- "excellent opportunity for [name] to"
- "continue building" (too developmental)
- "further strengthen" (too developmental)
- Any exclamation marks (!)
- Casual contractions

EXAMPLE PROFESSIONAL LANGUAGE: "John consistently demonstrated exceptional leadership capabilities throughout the review period. His strategic approach to the Q4 Product Initiative resulted in a 95% achievement score, significantly exceeding organizational objectives and delivering substantial value to the company's product roadmap. John's results-oriented approach and professional excellence in stakeholder engagement contributed significantly to the strategic initiative's success, demonstrating measurable impact on performance metrics."

{% elif tone == "encouraging" %}
**ENCOURAGING TONE - STRICT REQUIREMENTS:**

MANDATORY CHARACTERISTICS:
- Use warm, enthusiastic, supportive language throughout - MUST feel uplifting
- Address employee directly by name and express pride/excitement explicitly
- Use exclamation marks strategically (at least 1-2) to convey enthusiasm
- Focus on achievements and future potential with optimism
- Use first-person expressions: "I am proud," "I am impressed," "I am excited"
- Structure sentences to build momentum and positivity
- Use motivational language: "excellent," "remarkable," "outstanding," "fantastic," "inspiring"

REQUIRED PHRASES (must use at least 3-4):
- "I am truly impressed" / "I'm truly impressed"
- "I am proud of" / "I'm proud of"
- "remarkable achievement"
- "excellent work"
- "fantastic contribution"
- "inspiring performance"
- "looking forward to"
- "continue to excel"
- "building on your success"
- "great potential"
- "outstanding"

FORBIDDEN PHRASES (DO NOT USE):
- "demonstrated exceptional performance" (too formal/professional)
- "organizational objectives" (too corporate/professional)
- "strategic impact" (too formal/professional)
- "performance metrics" (too formal/professional)
- "opportunity to develop" (too developmental)
- "continue building" (too developmental)
- "further strengthen" (too developmental)
- Neutral, objective language

EXAMPLE ENCOURAGING LANGUAGE: "John, I am truly impressed with your remarkable achievement on the Q4 Product Initiative! Your excellent work not only exceeded expectations but also inspired the entire team. I am proud of your fantastic contribution and am looking forward to seeing you continue to excel in even more ambitious projects. Your inspiring performance demonstrates great potential, and I am excited about building on your success in the next review period!"

{% elif tone == "developmental" %}
