EXAMPLE DEVELOPMENTAL LANGUAGE: "John has shown strong performance in leadership and communication, with particular strength in team leadership. This review period presents an excellent opportunity for John to continue building his communication skills, particularly in stakeholder presentations. By further strengthening these capabilities, John can enhance his already impressive track record and grow in the area of complex project management. I see clear growth potential and am committed to supporting John's professional development through targeted training and mentorship opportunities."

{% elif tone == "concise" %}
**CONCISE TONE - STRICT REQUIREMENTS:**

MANDATORY CHARACTERISTICS:
- Use direct, brief, bullet-point style language - NO elaboration
- Keep sentences short (10-15 words maximum per sentence)
- Focus on facts and outcomes only - NO emotional language
- Use simple, straightforward vocabulary - NO complex business jargon
- Eliminate all unnecessary words and phrases
- Structure as brief statements separated by periods
- Use action verbs: "achieved," "demonstrated," "improved," "met," "exceeded"

